# Git — commit and push

When you finish a task that changes project files (and the user has not asked to skip version control), **commit with a clear message and push to `origin`** on the current branch so work is on the remote. If there is nothing to commit, do not force an empty commit.

If push fails (auth, conflicts), report the error and stop; do not overwrite remote history without explicit user instruction.
